35,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,The data shows we lose an hour daily copying records. It’s a silent drain.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,May,,"The coordination group is empty, yet two people write all logs by hand.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,Half the customer plants have no signal. Developer availability is zero until Q3.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Capital is frozen, but software allowance has room. Licences climb per head.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Kenji,,Tools needing daily entry from everyone were dropped. Narrow tools survived.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Kenji, that matches my finding. The daily friction kills broad tools.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, if developers are busy, we can't build complex things.","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, exactly. We can't rely on external help or internal devs right now.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Kenji, the software allowance is the only open pocket. We must use it.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Ryuji, agreed. We need a tool that fits the software allowance and survives.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@May, the manual logs are a symptom of the missing coordination staff.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, yes. We need a solution that doesn't add to their burden.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, the frozen capital means we can't buy new hardware or big builds.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, correct. We must stick to the recurring software allowance.","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@All, let's focus on what fits the software budget and avoids daily entry.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I agree. We need to minimize the daily effort on the floor.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,May,,I agree. We must protect the existing staff from extra manual work.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,I agree. We must avoid dependencies on unavailable developers or bad network.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,I agree. The software allowance is our only viable funding source.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Kenji,,I agree. We must pick a tool that has proven to survive its first year.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
